## Code Documentation Requirements

### Component Documentation

All components must include:

````typescript
/**
 * Component description in Australian English
 * @component ComponentName
 * @example
 * ```tsx
 * <ComponentName prop="value" />
 * ```
 * @accessibility
 * - ARIA roles: [list roles]
 * - Keyboard navigation: [describe]
 */
````

### TypeScript Documentation

```typescript
interface Props {
  /** Description of the prop in Australian English */
  requiredProp: string;
  /** Optional prop with default value */
  optionalProp?: string;
}
```

### CSS Documentation

```css
/* Component: Button
 * Purpose: Reusable button with multiple variants
 * Tokens: Uses var(--color-primary-main), var(--color-secondary-main)
 * Dark mode: Supported via :root[data-theme="dark"]
 */
.button {
  /* styles */
}
```

## Content Documentation

### Markdown Files

All markdown files must:

- Use Australian English spelling
- Follow first-person voice for Dale's content
- Include frontmatter with metadata
- Use proper heading hierarchy
- Include examples where appropriate

### Voice Guidelines Reference

When writing ANY content, follow: `docs/CONTENT_VOICE_GUIDELINES.md`

**Key Rules**:

- First person ("I help..." not "Dale helps...")
- Active voice (80%+)
- Australian English (organise, colour, centre)
- Confident without arrogance
- Practical over academic

## Documentation Updates

### When to Update Documentation

**ALWAYS update documentation when**:

- Adding new features
- Changing existing behavior
- Updating design system
- Modifying color palette
- Changing component interfaces
- Adding new patterns

### Documentation Files to Update

When making changes, consider updating:

- `README.md` - If project setup changes
- `CHANGELOG.md` - For all notable changes
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` - For architectural changes
- `docs/COMPONENTS.md` - For component changes
- `docs/THEME.md` - For theme/design changes
- Component-specific docs - For component updates

## Documentation Checklist

Before committing:

- [ ] Code comments added for complex logic
- [ ] Component documentation updated
- [ ] TypeScript types documented
- [ ] README updated (if needed)
- [ ] CHANGELOG updated
- [ ] Architecture docs updated (if needed)
- [ ] Australian English used throughout
- [ ] Examples provided where helpful
- [ ] Links to related documentation added

## Quality Standards

### Writing Style

- **Clear and concise**: Avoid unnecessary complexity
- **Australian English**: Use proper spelling and formatting
- **Consistent voice**: Follow voice guidelines
- **Scannable**: Use headings, bullets, short paragraphs
- **Examples**: Include practical examples

### Technical Accuracy

- **Code examples**: Must be valid and tested
- **Links**: Must be current and working
- **Screenshots**: Must be up-to-date
- **APIs**: Must match implementation

### Maintenance

- **Review quarterly**: Check for outdated content
- **Update on changes**: Keep docs in sync with code
- **Archive old docs**: Move outdated docs to archive
- **Version docs**: Tag docs with version numbers

